From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mckenna654 <mckenna654@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:38:24 +1100
Subject: Simple puzzles for Little Trainers

Spin tiles do not spin, Lt. Surge's gates are off, Cinnabar Gym is unlocked,
Victory Road's rock barriers are down, Silph Co.'s Card Key doors are open,
the Safari Zone has no step limit, and lifts open on the floor the current
story goal needs. The arrow leads up to Snorlax once the Poke Flute is owned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/include/little_trainers.h b/include/little_trainers.h
index 70fdc738e..55fe1f47c 100644
--- a/include/little_trainers.h
+++ b/include/little_trainers.h
@@ -49,6 +49,8 @@ struct LtRules
     // Exploring
     u8 encounterRatePercent;    // how often wild Pokemon appear (100 = original)
     bool8 navArrow;             // an arrow beside the player points along the way to the next story goal
+    bool8 simplePuzzles;        // gates that normally need a puzzle solved are already open, spin
+                                // tiles do not spin, lifts go where the story needs, no Safari step limit
     bool8 hmFree;               // Cut, Surf, Strength, Rock Smash and Waterfall work as soon as the
                                 // player owns the HM (no need to teach it); caves are never dark
 
@@ -128,6 +130,10 @@ void LT_DrawStartMenuIcon(u8 windowId, u8 startMenuItem, u8 y);
 // 8x8 heart tile for one slice of the HP bar with 0-8 of its pixels filled.
 const u8 *LT_HeartTile(u8 filledPixels);
 
+// Opens the story's puzzle gates for presets with simplePuzzles. Called on every map change,
+// before the map's own scripts decide what to draw.
+void LT_OpenPuzzleGates(void);
+
 // The "where do I go?" arrow (src/little_trainers_nav.c).
 void LT_Nav_Update(void);       // every frame on the field
 void LT_Nav_OnHeapReset(void);
